  "goodToKnow": "Die Konfirmation is confirmation in the Protestant church, usually at about 14, when young people confirm their baptism after a year of Konfirmandenunterricht. The Catholic equivalent is die Firmung, preceded by the Erstkommunion at about nine. In eastern Germany, the secular Jugendweihe remains popular. Confirmands traditionally receive generous gifts, often money. Plural: die Konfirmationen."
